{"title":"Northeastern WOOTers Mock AIME I Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be digits, not necessarily distinct and not necessarily non-zero. For how many quadruples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/e/9fe3200bc117ee29cf5ddf31161d761523aef996.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(u,v,x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> is it true that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/5/5250ca87064ef657283089d9ffad57c48304eecb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N = \\overline{uv.xy}+\\overline{xy.uv}\\]\" width=\"152\" height=\"16\" /> is an integer? As an example, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/a/17a22f42c61bbe660fdd064d68365b7f6a91e7bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(u,v,x,y)=(0,1,2,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"175\" height=\"18\" />, then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/eba395878d95792960c0658b13e23cf1a5365f93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 1.23 + 23.01 = 24.24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"202\" height=\"14\" />, which is not an integer.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"Northeastern WOOTers Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 1\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It is given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/1/d81a26aa68cdf61c6e59b9e8cf5cf4fc3ec0ba4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$181^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" /> can be written as the difference of the cubes of two consecutive positive integers.  Find the sum of these two integers. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"Northeastern WOOTers Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 2\"> Solution</a> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> be a triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb1b7b0526168d6f1aa059eaabc8b9ec9a3421ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afa9585319530527a9fbb662a7c350773e845bf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=112$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/2/e22b6d629989840964cf6b9bdcc818be7f00a5fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=113$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"79\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be trisection points on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. That is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/4/964e429b8bef009b3a2d742bc52dd78c414276e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX=XY=YB$\" width=\"138\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the points of intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/9/5895bfa441a2027d808cec50fa4da5229e07e89e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CX}$\" width=\"31\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/e/e0e730a98f5c74d99ad253902ba164219e8a9234.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CY}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> with the cevian <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41ee10c07baa91f100ec2eeca6b7b6ed3ab86698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AM}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />, respectively. Find the area of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/9/cc923f6cacf8e3e67f1e9809ee560570d5140239.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XYED$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Northeastern WOOTers Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\"> Solution</a> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the number of ordered tuples of positive odd integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/5/165324e8bf87081fc9788e182138f01a1336e522.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( x_1, x_2, \\cdots, x_{42} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/1/5915e01854f63560c1adf9235b7319f1280e6ab1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_1 + x_2 + \\cdots + x_{42} = 2014\\]\" width=\"208\" height=\"15\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Northeastern WOOTers Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\"> Solution</a> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be real numbers. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5dbfe732cf4879ca7647d91ad0860229ee0436d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+2y^2+3z^2=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />, the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/f/41fcae6e0b0c7f3f9ee2755f339602ce70e10ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( 3x+2y+z \\right)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"21\" /> can be represented <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"Northeastern WOOTers Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 5\"> Solution</a> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/a/44a05dd0756958cc560bd1fd3e757b60b8855b0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{S}=\\{1,...,10\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" />. Two subsets, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> are chosen randomly with replacement, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> chosen after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.  The probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is a subset of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/e/1fe098aff35602f71788bb7b0529940566e4ab40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {p^a}{q^b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"19\" height=\"40\" />, for some primes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84e2ea73aa1d9541a7b24b1228d852ed05b24cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab+p+q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"Northeastern WOOTers Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 6\"> Solution</a> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/0/d50a2d431c19da14a1315bafce20a96fbad235af.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{n=0}^{100}\\left\\lfloor\\frac{3n+4}{13}\\right\\rfloor-\\left\\lfloor\\frac{n-28+\\left\\lfloor\\frac{n-7}{13}\\right\\rfloor}{4}\\right\\rfloor.\\]\" width=\"279\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"Northeastern WOOTers Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 7\"> Solution</a> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Dai the Luzon bleeding-heart has numbered lillypads, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. Then, Ryan the alligator eats those lillypads with the intention of eating Dai. Dai starts on a random lillypad and flies around between lillypads randomly every minute. Ryan also eats a random lillypad every minute. If the expected number of minutes left for Dai to live is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"Northeastern WOOTers Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 8\"> Solution</a> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> be a regular hexagon of unit side length. Line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f32db217d7630882c3441fa8821cd70a6958c3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> is extended to a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> outside of the hexagon such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/b/18b5435d18a9be1686097352cbf2ecb8424023ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FP=\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />. The line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/1/b41699a79262163c0df579406c575f506f6dfb97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> intersects the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/a/0aa4ad1cf6a0ad719767e1739c9b689debc60142.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BF}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0f6a692f19a65fe60fe5745826792f3fd1d57e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{EF}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Let the area of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/0/3d02df4d7a299e2a20dca06d58e650d16442197e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BENM$\" width=\"65\" height=\"12\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. Then, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/7/c376a77363ce51081c8bae497075069580499085.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S^2$\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/3/8d3b316934173cb96039c655080619cd9f60715e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)); string label[]={&#39;A&#39;,&#39;B&#39;,&#39;C&#39;,&#39;D&#39;,&#39;E&#39;,&#39;F&#39;}; pair hex[]; for(int i=0;i&lt;=5;i=i+1) { hex[i]=dir(180-60*i);  if(i!=4) label(&quot;$&quot;+label[i]+&quot;$&quot;,hex[i],dir((0,0)--hex[i])); else label(&quot;$E$&quot;,hex[4],dir(240)); } draw(hex[0]--hex[1]--hex[2]--hex[3]--hex[4]--hex[5]--cycle); pair X=2.25*hex[4]; draw(hex[1]--X); draw(X--hex[5],linetype(&quot;4 4&quot;)); [/asy]\" width=\"272\" height=\"335\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Northeastern WOOTers Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\"> Solution</a> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> are complex numbers such that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/09687f1d076b98142ff3ae48c0eafff8c1814610.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*} \\frac{1}{a-b}+\\frac{1}{b-c}+\\frac{1}{c-a}&amp;=&amp;0,\\\\ \\text{and} \\qquad \\frac{a\\overline{b}+b\\overline{c}+c\\overline{a}-\\overline{a}b-\\overline{b}c-\\overline{c}a}{\\left(a-b\\right)\\left(\\overline{a-b}\\right)}&amp;=&amp;k, \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"337\" height=\"94\" />\nthen find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/4/25486ef28067fab2192c0f5b307954cca75c93ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^4$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"Northeastern WOOTers Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 10\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Cody and Toedy play a game. Cody guesses an integer between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/7/16794ed8d576bcdfc1b48ac2155ce53ff11aff25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2014$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> inclusive, and then Toedy guesses a different integer. A 2014-sided die is rolled. After rolling, whoever guessed closest to the number on the die wins. The winning player wins as much money as the number rolled. Assuming both players play optimally, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the number should Cody guess to maximize his earnings. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Northeastern WOOTers Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\"> Solution</a> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> be a triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/c/fbc280b5d1be327bba340fc651a9831273fd9066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=39$\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/4/954b59f68715d6a48181e3a8e7dcacee9093c4fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/4/5044d71e5472ca7df9c6ffd0b4c25180f9d1d3cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA=45$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />.  A point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is placed on the extension of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> past <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee48e5d3968014ef1e27c31e56d2f7ea5f8cb1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> be the circumcenters of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> respectively.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/a/29aaff1c41b587163dade25e211571b87fbec119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1O_2=29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" />, then the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ea589dbdb3eee7b276b3bfdbb62e1668995762.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BD}{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"32\" height=\"37\" /> can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" /> for relatively prime positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.  Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Northeastern WOOTers Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 12 (page does not exist)\"> Solution</a> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define a <i>T-Polyomino</i> to be a set of 4 cells in a grid that form a T, as shown below. Dai wants to place T-Polyominos onto a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/d/62d4eeb6a966219df4ac79cfc9981ec095e6be0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> grid such that there is no overlap. He continues to place T-Polyominos randomly until he can no longer do so. Let the probability that he will cover the entire board be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/2/a32dbdb15739866df92edf7c4bff82c5f7006b99.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(100); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)); draw(origin--(0,1)--(3,1)--(3,0)--cycle^^(1,1)--(1,-1)--(2,-1)--(2,1)); [/asy]\" width=\"168\" height=\"112\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Northeastern WOOTers Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 13 (page does not exist)\"> Solution</a> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider three infinite sequences of real numbers: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/9/339a92a7d26235d4afec3fc297beb249735b9769.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*} X &amp;=&amp; \\left( x_1, x_2, \\cdots \\right), \\\\ Y &amp;=&amp; \\left( y_1, y_2, \\cdots \\right), \\\\ Z &amp;=&amp; \\left( z_1, z_2, \\cdots \\right). \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"161\" height=\"68\" /> It is known that, for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, the following statement holds: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/8/e68fd724cd230388581f0d6a956f1ccf675413eb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\left( \\left( \\log_2 x_n \\right)^2 + \\left( \\log_2 y_n \\right)^2 \\right) \\cdot \\left( \\left( \\log_2 y_n \\right)^2 + \\left( \\log_2 z_n \\right)^2 \\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\left( \\log_2 x_n \\log_2 y_n + \\log_2 y_n \\log_2 z_n \\right)^2.\\end{align*}\" width=\"681\" height=\"60\" />The elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are defined by the relation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/f/a4fe693d416d010d5db0496eab490109c6a32ff5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_n=2^{\\frac{n}{2^n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"21\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/c/fcc4de4018e5c4749888ad5b640d52d82f38f575.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S =\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\log_2 x_n \\log_2 y_n \\log_2 z_n.\\]\" width=\"231\" height=\"48\" />Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> can be represented as a fraction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"Northeastern WOOTers Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 14\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the sum of all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/6/db68e8a2aef3038cdc7576a07fba22e4de36d0ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\le96$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/7/2278d67dcf2c3f9a73967961071ed4672ca776ae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\phi(n)&gt;n-\\sqrt{n},\\]\" width=\"123\" height=\"19\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/a/edae70ddedf89e790936ed4035c5ca1480212e0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the number of integers less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that are relatively prime to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Northeastern_WOOTers_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"Northeastern WOOTers Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 15\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018101630\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.047 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.074 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 678/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 23124/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12807:|#|:idhash:canonical and